prompt:
You are a formal verification assistant. The following Dafny program fails Dafny verification.

=== PROGRAM ===
method twoSum(nums: array<int>, target: int) returns (i: int, j: int)
  requires nums.Length > 1
  requires exists i,j::0 <= i < j < nums.Length &&  nums[i] + nums[j] == target
  ensures 0 <= i < j < nums.Length && nums[i] + nums[j] == target
  ensures forall ii,jj:: (0 <= ii < i && ii < jj < nums.Length)  ==> nums[ii] + nums[jj] != target
  ensures forall jj:: i < jj < j ==> nums[i] + nums[jj] != target
{
  var n := nums.Length;
  i := 0;
  j := 1;
  while i < n - 1
    invariant 0 <= i < j <= n
    invariant forall ii, jj :: 0 <= ii < i && ii < jj < n ==> nums[ii] + nums[jj] != target
  {
    j := i + 1;
    while j < n
      invariant 0 <= i < j <= (n) + 1
      invariant forall jj :: i < jj < j ==> nums[i] + nums[jj] != target
    {
      if nums[i] + nums[j] == target {
        return;
      }
      j := j + 1;
    }

    i := i + 1;
  }
}

=== DAFNY ERROR ===
program.dfy(12,25): Error: this invariant could not be proved to be maintained by the loop
 Related message: loop invariant violation

program.dfy(18,58): Error: index out of range

Dafny program verifier finished with 1 verified, 2 errors

=== COUNTEREXAMPLE ===
For the error at line 12: At initial state: nums.Length = 1847, nums[1361] = 8365, nums[1398] = 1796, nums[609] = 1346, target = 10161. At a program state: n = 1847. At a program state: i = 0. At a program state: j = 1.
For the error at line 18: At initial state: nums.Length = 1238, nums[752] = 8365, nums[789] = 1796, target = 10161. At a program state: n = 1238. At a program state: i = 0. At a program state: j = 1.

Analyze the failure and respond with ONLY a valid JSON object — no explanation, no markdown, no code fences. Use exactly this structure:

{
  "spec_element": "<one of: requires | invariant | ensures>",
  "proof_obligation": "<one of: initiation | preservation | bridge>",
  "diagnosis": "<explanation of what broke and why>",
  "repair": "<the corrected Dafny specification line that restores the intended behavior>"
